    "Model tends to underestimate prices in the short term (1-3 days) after a downward trend, especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly negative.",
    "Overestimates prices following spikes, particularly in the 1-5 day window after a sharp increase, suggesting overshoot bias.",
    "Underestimates prices in the 7-14 day horizon when sentiment is neutral, indicating mean reversion bias toward higher levels.",
    "When sentiment is positive (e.g., >0.25), model tends to lag behind true price movements, requiring a 1-2 day adjustment upward.",
    "In the 15-30 day horizon, model consistently underestimates true prices, suggesting a systematic bias toward lower values — correct by adding 2-5% of the recent 7-day average to forecast.",
    "Avoid overfitting to recent highs; if last 3 days show a spike, reduce forecast by 10-15% for next 3 days to prevent overshoot."
  ]
